{
    "$comment": "The namespaces each page route inlines into its HTML, by route id (routes.ts); /settings/:section has one entry per section (settings:section:<section>). The root's go with every page, so they hold only what any page may show (settings: the Settings nav, autosave status and home widget other modules render too; shell and chat.nav: the header, the sidebar, the error pages and the chat's loading state); a route's only with its own. shell:signed-out is the sign-in screen's, which the shell's loader inlines signed out and for a one-time link. Namespaces only a dialog opened by a click, a card below the fold or a client-only panel needs (settings.dialogs, settings.person-dialogs, settings.workspace-limits, -apps, -github, -rooms, -setup; settings.devices on a person's page; shell.palette, shell.help (the theme's words too), shell.add-device, shell.status; chat.report, chat.result, chat.drafts; pages.dialogs, pages.cover, pages.review, and pages.editor, the page editor's, which a page's clientLoader starts with the route's data) are in no entry, and the live chat's (chat.composer, chat.model, chat.trace; client-only) only where a page shows them on the server: they load on demand (i18n/on-demand.tsx). scripts/i18n-build.mjs reports each route's size against the budget.",
